.TH "vsearch-udbinfo" "1" "April 29, 2026" "version 2.31.0" "vsearch manual"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
vsearch --udbinfo \[em] show information about a UDB database file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]vsearch\f[R] \f[B]--udbinfo\f[R] \f[I]udbfile\f[R]
[\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The vsearch command \f[V]--udbinfo\f[R] reads a UDB database file and
writes information about it to the \f[I]standard error\f[R]
\f[V]stderr(3)\f[R].
The information includes the number of sequences (Seqs), the number of
bits per sequence index entry (SeqIx bits), the alphabet (Alpha), the
word length used for the index (Word width), the number of index slots
(Slots), the dictionary size (Dict size), and the DBstep and DBAccel
settings.
Masking information is not stored in UDB files and is therefore not
reported.
.PP
See \f[V]vsearch-udb(5)\f[R] for a description of the UDB file format.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS mandatory options
.TP
\f[V]--udbinfo\f[R] \f[I]udbfile\f[R]
Read and inspect the UDB database \f[I]udbfile\f[R].
This option is mandatory.
As UDB files cannot be read from pipes, \f[I]udbfile\f[R] must be a
seekable file path (see \f[V]vsearch-udb(5)\f[R]); a pipe is rejected
with an error.
.SS secondary options
.TP
\f[V]--log\f[R] \f[I]filename\f[R]
Write messages to \f[I]filename\f[R].
Messages include program version, start and finish times, elapsed time,
amount of memory available, maximum amount of memory consumed, number of
cores and command line options, and if need be, command-specific
informational messages, warnings, and errors.
.TP
\f[V]--quiet\f[R]
Suppress messages to the \f[I]standard output\f[R] \f[V]stdout(3)\f[R]
and \f[I]standard error\f[R] \f[V]stderr(3)\f[R], except for warnings
and error messages.
.SS ignored options
.TP
\f[V]--threads\f[R] \f[I]positive non-null integer\f[R]
Command is not multithreaded, option has no effect (a warning is printed
when more than one thread is requested).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Display information about a UDB database:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
vsearch \[rs]
    --udbinfo db.udb
\f[R]
.fi
